fluidaudio-rs — keeper fork
===========================

This directory is keeper's fork of fluidaudio-rs, the Rust bindings for
FluidAudio by FluidInference:

  upstream: https://github.com/FluidInference/fluidaudio-rs
  forked from: main @ bd1f0f36cb7d43e8a564b38dc01eb365864b3b79 (2026-07-23,
               crate version 0.14.8)
  license: MIT (declared in the upstream Cargo.toml and README; upstream ships
           no LICENSE file, so LICENSE here is the standard MIT text naming
           FluidInference)

It links FluidAudio (https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio,
Apache-2.0) at 0.17.4, revision 21493f8dac5a97e65742e6ff26f42f164c2fda0f,
without its NemoTextProcessing trait.

What keeper changed
-------------------
- FluidAudio 0.14.8 -> 0.17.4 (exact), SwiftPM tools 6.2, Swift 5 language
  mode, the NeMo text-normalization binary target dropped (`traits: []`).
- The Swift bridge was rewritten around keeper's needs:
  - Parakeet TDT v3 (int8) loads from a caller-named directory through
    `AsrModels.loadLocal`, and the pyannote community-1 offline diarizer is
    built from `MLModel(contentsOf:)` per model plus the PLDA parameters.
    Neither path reaches FluidAudio's download, prepare or purge helpers; the
    Rust side refuses a directory with missing files before calling Swift.
  - Recognition takes an optional language (Parakeet's token-language filter)
    and returns token timings and confidences; diarization takes samples and
    returns segments plus per-speaker embeddings; a single-clip embedding
    call returns the dominant speaker's vector.
  - Audio tracks are listed and decoded (one track or all mixed, optional time
    range) to 16 kHz mono f32 with AVAssetReader, which reads `.mov` files
    with video that AVAudioFile cannot open.
  - Results cross the boundary as JSON strings freed by
    `fluidaudio_free_string`; errors carry the Swift error text instead of
    being printed.
  - The engine handle is a retained object per `FluidAudio` value (no
    process-global bridge); the Rust type is `Send` but not `Sync` and every
    call takes `&mut self`, so one owner runs one model at a time.
- Removed: VAD, streaming and sliding-window ASR, Qwen3-ASR, Sortformer,
  Kokoro TTS, ITN, system-info calls, examples, tests fixtures, CI and
  release workflows, feature flags.
- build.rs builds only for a macOS target (the crate's pure-Rust part
  compiles anywhere), passes `--arch`, and adds the Swift runtime search
  paths.
